	abstract = {This research proposes a smart farming platform that integrates Internet of Things (IoT), machine learning (ML), and cloud-native microservices to en-hance agricultural productivity and sustainability. The system collects real-time environmental and soil data—such as temperature, humidity, and soil moisture through IoT sensors and processes it using ML algorithms for predictive analytics. These models provide intelligent recommendations for crop management, including irrigation, fertilization, and pest control, improving decision-making from sowing to harvesting. The platform is developed using the MERN stack for both frontend and backend, and deployed on Amazon Web Services (AWS), utilizing EC2, S3, and Lambda for scalable compute and storage solutions. Containerization is handled through Docker, with orchestration managed by Kubernetes, allowing efficient deployment and seamless scalability. A built-in anomaly detection module identifies early signs of threats such as pest outbreaks or abrupt environmental changes, helping to minimize crop losses. Real-time insights support precise resource utilization, livestock monitoring, and early threat mitigation. The system’s advanced analytics capabilities enable accurate yield estimation, weather forecasting, and market trend analysis, empowering farmers with data-driven decisions. Designed to be scalable and modular, the platform serves farms of all sizes, promoting resilience and long-term sustainability in agriculture. © Grenze Scientific Society, 2025.},
