	abstract = {The rapid growth of cloud-native applications has increased the need for real-time data processing systems that can continuously collect, process, analyse, and respond to high-volume data streams with low latency. Traditional batch-based processing processes fail to perform well in modern cloud environments, as these processes analyze data after some delay and cannot support real-time decision-making for time-sensitive operations. The well-established real-time processing solutions also have some drawbacks like scalability concerns, deployment complexity, delay in analytical response, and restricted support of intelligent prediction models. To address the challenges, this paper proposed an intelligent monitoring and decision support system for cloud-native applications based on real-time data processing with Azure Stream Analytics and Azure Machine Learning integrated with the cloud. The proposed framework gathers the streaming data from various sources like IoT devices, web applications, APIs, sensors, application logs, and business transaction systems. These collected events are then piped into Azure Event Hubs or Azure IoT Hub and processed with Azure Stream Analytics for filtering, transforming, aggregating, and analyzing based on queries. After the stream data has been processed, it is transformed into meaningful features, which are then used to train machine learning models for stream classification, anomaly detection, failure prediction, and generating alerts. The experimental results verify that the proposed model can classify the conditions Normal-Stream, Delayed-Stream, and Anomaly-Detected with an overall accuracy of 97%. The results show the combination of Azure Stream Analytics and machine learning as a way to enhance real-time monitoring, make decisions faster, optimize resources, and provide intelligent automated responses in cloud-native scenarios. © 2026 IEEE.},
